## Batch 3 — Delete + Trash
**Script:** `npm run test:cms:batch3` | headed: `npm run test:cms:batch3:headed`
**Workers:** variable per phase (see below)
**Estimated time:** ~32 min
**GHA:** `cms-batch3-scheduled.yml` — auto-triggers via `workflow_run` after Batch 2 completes

**Order:** LIFO — content before structure, structure before stack, stack always last, trash after all deletes.

Phases run strictly sequentially (Phase N waits for Phase N-1 to complete). Within each phase, workers are set for optimal parallelism:

| Phase | Group | Flows | Workers | Ordering rule |
|-------|-------|-------|---------|---------------|
| 1 | Content | 10 | 5 | All independent |
| 2 | Taxonomy | 2 | 1 | term → taxonomy (strict) |
| 3 | Structure | 2 | 2 | global-field + content-type independent |
| 4 | Releases | 2 | 2 | Independent |
| 5 | Services | 6 | 3 | tokens/webhook/workflows mostly independent |
| 6 | Branches | 2 | 1 | alias → branch (strict) |
| 7 | Env/Lang | 2 | 2 | Independent |
| 8 | Users/Roles | 2 | 2 | Independent |
| 9 | Stack | 3 | 1 | leave → transfer → delete (strict — always last delete) |
| 10 | Trash | 8 | 7 | All restores independent |

**Total: 38 flows (30 delete + 8 trash)**

